In article <7tc7h0$68e$1@coco.singnet.com.sg>, Matthew Tan
<tankc@singnet.com.sg> wrote:
>I am an X-Windows newbie, so thanks for any help.
>
>Currently I can open an xterm with my Reflection. But when I tried to run X
>windows application such as xcalc, I would get an error message :
>
>Error: Can't open display:

You most likely need to define the environment variable DISPLAY.  For
example:

        setenv DISPLAY hostname.mumble.com:0.0
or
        setenv DISPLAY host:0.0

When you started your xterm the local window manager most likely
started the command with the -display option on the xterm command line,
so this is how your xterm worked correctly but your xcalc did not.



