Two security questions relating to DU 4.0E:


(1) The online security manual for DU 4.0E says (in section 10.14) that
it is possible to have login failures logged to the system log. 
However, I can't seem to figure out how to enable this.  All I currently
get in the logs are attempts (both failed and successful) to become the
superuser.  I  have /etc/syslog.conf set to "debug" level for everything
except daemon... shouldn't that catch these events?  The security manual
says "see the system administration manual" for more info, but I don't
see anything in that manual except a cross-reference back to the
security manual.



(2) Unable to solve (1), I set up the auditing system for testing on
several of our machines.  I am trying to get the auditds on each machine
to forward their data to one machine.  But the machine I'm telling them
to send to is reporting "host XXX failed access check to auditd master"
in its /var/audit/auditd_cons file whenever they try to connect.  I got
one of our other machines to work, using the same options in rc.config
and the same list of allowed hosts in /etc/sec/auditd_clients, and the
same permissions on that file on both machines.  

I assume this may be some type of general security setting somewhere,
because this same machine also refuses to let any machine (including
_itself_) connect to its advfsd using dtadvfs.  This is despite the
correct entries in /var/opt/advfsd/socket/hosts.allow -- entries that I
know are correct because when I use the exact same entries on a
different machine everything is fine.  In this case the advfsd log
reports "AUDIT | WARNING - failed security check | File socket_agent.c |
line 573".




-- 
