Nico van Vliet (N.vanVliet@wb.utwente.nl) wrote:
: Do you have the same experience with the 'ar' command? Or better still,
: do you know a solution?

Yes, and maybe. It looks like ar uses a whole bunch of small I/O
requests to read in the original archive and then to write out
a new copy of it, with the new file(s) added. This works fine 
as long as the unified buffer cache is large enough to hold both 
copies, but suffers horribly when it isn't.

Two possible solutions: the first one is to install more memory
and/or tune up the ubc size (see the system configuration and
tuning guide); the second solution is to rewrite your makefiles
to add as much files to the archive as you can in a single go.

Cheers,

/Serge.P

