I have updated my DEC UNIX from version 4.0A (on AlphaStation 500) to
4.0B and then to 4.0D and now I have a problem that X-server does not
start any more.

In file /usr/var/dt/Xerrors there is a following note:

Fatal server error:
Failed to establish all listening sockets


error (pid 530): Server unexpectedly died


error (pid 530): Server for display :0 can't be started


If I use ps -ef to find out pid 530 I get

root 530 1 0.0 18:08:52 ?? 0:00.28 /usr/dt/bin/dtlogin -daemon



During the update from B->D I got message:

"cron may not be running - call your system administrator"  

when system was merging files /usr/var/spool/cron/crontabs/.new.root and
.proto.root. Has this something to do with my problem ?

Thanks,

Karri Honkoila, karri.honkoila@fortum.com



